{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>דרכיו ראיתי.</b> Now this is a sign of the correctness of the interpretation of the book: as when 'I saw his ways,' or that he repented, or its meaning is like 'for the inclination of man's heart is evil' (Genesis 8:21):" "<b>וארפאהו.</b> For he was like a sick person, for a sick person has no strength to walk:" "<b>ואשלם נחומים לו.</b> That I comfort him over the illness that had befallen him:" "<b>ולאבליו.</b> They are his loved ones, like mourners over a sick person at his death:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:01.852259318Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}